d "bdc8b2c9-de7b-5b6a-8d60-6e3dd551afe2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500279 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186499660 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500279 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186499804 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500279 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186499825 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500279 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186499910 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500279 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186499991 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500279 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500279 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500279 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186499910 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500279 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "ffacf0a3-cce6-5d50-befc-250fcc891555" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500329 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186500279 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500329 #edb/ref 1069 "q-111515" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500329 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500329 #edb/ref 1071 "The matrix $V$ is given below. Let ${v}_{1}$, ${v}_{2}$,  ${v}_{3}$, and ${v}_{4}$ be the respective columns of $V.$ Determine if $B=\\text{{}{v}_{1},{v}_{2}\\text{}}$ is a basis of $\\text{Col}(V).$ If that is the case, find ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}$, where ${v}_{4}={x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}.$\n\n$$\nV=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -2 & -3 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 6 & 8 & 12\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186500329 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "94724c66-b6e2-52f7-8122-f7efcf9307aa" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500329 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we reduce the matrix $V$ to reduced row echelon form (RREF):\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -2 & -3 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 6 & 8 & 12\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -2 & -6 \\\\ -2 & 6 & 8 & 12\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -2 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 6 & 6 & 18\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :=(-\\frac{1}{2}){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 6 & 6 & 18\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-6){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the matrix above, we see that the pivot columns are the $1$st and $2$nd columns. So, a basis of $\\text{Col}(V)$ is $\\{{v}_{1},{v}_{2}\\},$ that is to say,\n\n$$\nB=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}\\}.\n$$\n\nNow, since the $4$th column of the reduced matrix is a non-pivot column, then the entries in that column tell us the coefficients needed to express ${v}_{4}$ as a linear combination of all the other columns in the original matrix. So, we have\n\n$$\n{{\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 12\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{{v}_{4}}={{(3)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{1}}\\cdot {{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{{v}_{1}}+{{(3)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{2}}\\cdot {{\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{{v}_{2}}.\n$$\n\nThis gives us ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=3\\cdot 3=9.$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186500406 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "5c3d8e97-0b51-5cb8-8192-ccdedb866e30" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500406 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186247232 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500410 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186500413 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500410 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "6a505530-0125-5aa1-b8fc-29e02176aebb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500410 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186484219 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500413 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186500406 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500413 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "75a59557-04eb-59d6-9b2e-ff439f6bfe2e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500413 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186500329 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500435 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186500439 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186500435 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "ad58dfe